4	// csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_vit_megakernel.cuh — PHASE 2 of the TRUE L3 fused
5	// megakernel. ONE persistent kernel per training step runs the REAL Vision-
6	// Transformer forward+backward AND the optimizer math, separated only by
7	// in-kernel grid barriers — real model math, real optimizer math, ZERO
8	// intermediate kernel launches. The ViT counterpart of PHASE 1's
9	// fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh.
10	//
11	// This composes:
12	//   * the REAL ViT fwd/bwd stages (model_stage_vit.cuh — transcribed
13	//     line-for-line from the verified PyTorch oracle, asserted bit-identical to
14	//     autograd, and structurally mirrored on CPU),
15	//   * the existing persistent substrate (megakernel_common.cuh: task queue, the
16	//     hand-built sense-reversing GridBarrier),
17	//   * the existing REAL optimizer tail (opt_components.cuh::apply_optimizer<Opt>).
18	//
19	// STAGE / BARRIER LAYOUT (identical to the decoder — 5 phases, B0..B2 + the
20	// fused sync_reset; see the per-stage comments):
21	//   P0  each CTA zeroes its OWN grad-partial slice + loss slot.
22	//   --- grid barrier B0 ---
23	//   P1  BATCH-PARALLEL fwd+bwd: each CTA owns a FIXED contiguous batch slice (by
24	//       blockIdx.x), processes its samples ONE AT A TIME (CTA-cooperative),
25	//       accumulating each sample's weight-grad into the CTA's partial with a
26	//       single-owner-thread-per-element rule (no atomics → deterministic), and
27	//       sums its slice's NLL (fp32).
28	//   --- grid barrier B1 ---
29	//   P2  DETERMINISTIC cross-CTA reduce: sum partial[0..nCTA) in ASCENDING CTA
30	//       index into the global grad (no float atomics; order fixed → reuses the
31	//       work-steal queue to pick WHO reduces which tensor). Loss: fp64 ordered
32	//       sum → loss/B → a device float the host reads back (by CTA 0).
33	//   --- grid barrier B2 (sync_reset: also resets the queue for P3) ---
34	//   P3  the REAL apply_optimizer<Opt> tail consumes the reduced grad in place.
35	//
36	// DYNAMIC SHARED MEMORY (the ONE thing the decoder path did NOT need): ViT's
37	// per-sample VitSampleSmem is ≈ 183.67 KB (seq=17), which CANNOT be a static
38	// __shared__ (48 KB cap). So this kernel declares `extern __shared__` and the
39	// LAUNCHER must, all three of: (1) cudaFuncSetAttribute(kernel,
40	// cudaFuncAttributeMaxDynamicSharedMemorySize, sizeof(VitSampleSmem)); (2) pass
41	// dynamicSMemBytes=sizeof(VitSampleSmem) to cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMSM
42	// (so the occ≥1 hang-freedom check is honest); (3) pass it at <<<...>>>. Missing
43	// ANY of these makes the kernel silently fail to launch — see the launcher.
44	//
45	// HONESTY: no placeholder math anywhere on this path. fp32 compute is the
46	// correctness baseline; a bf16-compute follow-up would be a flag defaulting to
47	// THIS fp32 path (not yet wired — see the report / TODO in model_stage_vit.cuh).
48	// ============================================================================
